new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..e2c60f9ff4c1992da876ef8f9e6de40ec087b62a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/geoip-mmdb.md
@@ -0,0 +1,97 @@
+# GeoIP from a checked MMDB file
+
+The collector now uses `mmdb-lib` 3.0.3 with a single City MMDB file. It no longer
+ships the old five-file GeoIP dataset, CSV converter or `geoip-lite` dependency.
+The small files in `test/fixtures/geoip/` are synthetic test data and must never
+be configured for a public dashboard.
+
+## Collector settings
+
+| Setting | Required value |
+| --- | --- |
+| `GEOIP_MODE` | `mmdb` or `disabled`; always explicit |
+| `GEOIP_DATABASE_FILE` | In MMDB mode, an absolute path to the approved file |
+| `GEOIP_DATABASE_SHA256` | In MMDB mode, its approved 64-character lowercase SHA-256 |
+| `GEOIP_MAX_BYTES` | In MMDB mode, a positive byte budget no larger than 2147483647 |
+
+For intentional operation without geography, set `GEOIP_MODE=disabled` and omit
+all three database settings. Nodes still appear and report normally; flags and
+map points are unavailable. A misspelled mode, missing required setting,
+contradictory disabled configuration or legacy `GEODATADIR` stops startup.
+Persistence and API processes do not read a GeoIP file or need these settings.
+
+MMDB mode checks that the file is regular, nonempty, within budget, stable during
+reading and matches the configured hash before constructing the reader. A
+symlink at the final file component is refused; an immutable release directory
+selected through a parent directory symlink is supported. The reader then
+requires an IPv4/IPv6 `GeoLite2-City` or `GeoIP2-City` database in MMDB 2.0 format,
+with usable tree and build metadata. Missing or invalid configured data stops
+startup before sockets are created. There is no packaged-data fallback.
+
+After setting those environment variables, validate without starting a server:
+
+```sh
+node deploy/validate-geoip.cjs
+```
+
+Success prints JSON with the mode and accepted file metadata: hash, byte count,
+database type and build time, or `database: null` when explicitly disabled.
+Failure writes a diagnostic to stderr and exits nonzero. The old directory and
+byte-limit arguments are no longer supported. Validation does not download,
+modify, activate or refresh a dataset.
+
+The expected hash must come from the reviewed staging/release process. Computing
+a hash from arbitrary downloaded bytes and immediately trusting it does not
+establish provenance. The byte budget limits the input buffer; it is not a total
+process-memory limit. The metadata build date is reported, not a freshness
+policy. This loader does not comprehensively validate every MMDB pointer or
+provide resource isolation for an untrusted decoder input.
+
+## Lookup and display
+
+The collector looks up the admitted node's connection address, validates the IP
+syntax first and retains the complete IPv6/mapped address. Peer-reported
+geography is not accepted. The node model receives the collector's result,
+without loading its own database or repeating the lookup.
+
+Only the location country and valid coordinates enter the dashboard. A known
+country without coordinates retains its flag, with `ll: null` and no map point.
+Missing geography remains `null`; absent coordinates are never filled with
+zero. Explicit valid `[0, 0]` is preserved. The account's registered country is
+not substituted for a missing location country. IP geography remains approximate.
+
+The running process holds an immutable buffer. Changing the selected path does
+not refresh a live reader. Stage and verify a new immutable file, update the
+configured hash/path together, then use a supervised restart and lookup check.
+Rollback selects the previous approved file/hash and restarts again. The
+protected acquisition job, fresh production-data acceptance, refresh/deletion
+policy and supervision remain deployment work; none is scheduled here.
+
+If geography is enabled at launch, select the source/edition, account and
+applicable attribution/retention terms before using real data. For GeoLite2,
+retain the MaxMind attribution. An explicitly disabled launch does not need a
+GeoIP account or update job. The [earlier updater investigation](geoip-operations.md)
+and [legacy validator report](geoip-validation.md) remain historical evidence;
+their old conversion/validation commands are not the current deployment path.
+
+## Local acceptance
+
+Linux Node 24.21.0/npm 10.9.0 clean installation and backend audit pass with zero
+reported advisories. The dependency change removes eleven old package entries
+and adds the dependency-free reader; all other locked entries are unchanged.
+The install still reports the inherited v1-lock and `yaeti` deprecation notices.
+
+- 204 backend contracts, including 25 MMDB cases and the country-only snapshot case.
+- All 14 existing socket tests and 23 frontend tests.
+- Frontend lint and the normal deployment build, without build warnings.
+- Twelve compiled-browser checkpoints, including flags without coordinates,
+  mixed geography, unknown geography and the existing outage/recovery behavior.
+- Native efsn through WSS, disposable PostgreSQL, HTTPS API and browser with MMDB
+  enabled; the existing four native browser checkpoints pass.
+
+The obsolete validator's 59 cases are removed with its implementation, not
+silently skipped. Initial runner/fixture failures are retained in the parent
+investigation evidence: npm initially lacked Node on PATH, a numeric-limit test
+included the new mode setting, and the native harness parsed its readiness file
+before the producer finished writing it. The corrected runs pass. No efsn
+source, chain database, signing key or consensus rule was changed.
